        <body>
            <div xml:id="d387">

                <pb facs="0499" n="391" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg391"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Coombs to Mr.
                            Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tokio Japan</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-01-20"><hi rendition="#italic">January 20, 1893</hi></date>.
                        (Received February 23.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 81.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith copy
                    of a note of date the 19th instant from his excellency Mutsu Munemitsu, His
                    Imperial Japanese Majesty’s minister for foreign affairs, and of its two
                    accompaniments, relative to the receipt and disposition by the villagers of
                    Shiwaki-ura of the gift of $350 from the Government of the United States, in
                    recognition of their services in connection with the rescue of the crew of the
                    American merchant vessel <hi rendition="#italic">North American</hi>.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank L. Coombs.</hi></signed></closer>





